      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4480179591": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-27T18:54:56.089348+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "HIRING: Staff Backend Engineer, Node & TypeScript, Stable SportsTech Co, Used by Millions\nRECRUITER OVERVIEW:\nHey, I'm Will — Rumor has it I'm Colorado's #1 Most Connected, Respected & Bald-est 👨 🦲 #DevRecruiter™. As an agency software engineering recruiter, my team and I are actively and continually partnered with an ever-growing rolodex of private & public tech companies, as well as VC backed and self-funded startups, Pre-Seed through Acquisition/IPO...🚀 What these companies have in common is that they ALL are looking to Hire \" Uncommonly Good \" Founding, Mid, Senior, Lead, Staff & Principal Software Devs ... and of course, the Leaders of these Software Development Teams.\nA LITTLE ABOUT THE COMPANY\nMy client is a leading remote-first sports technology company with an enviable, collaborative, remote 1st culture. Their platform supports millions of users and tens of thousands of amateur sports organizations. Their engineering organization builds highly scalable, service-oriented, and event-driven systems using modern cloud technologies, APIs, databases, queues, caching, and observability tooling. I'm working directly with the CTO and 5 members of her team to hire 3 Devs: a Mid, a Senior, and a Staff ... This is a new client of mine, but maybe already my favorite company to work with :)\nWHY WORK WITH THIS COMPANY?\nSuper cool industry: They serve the Amateur Sports / SportsTech space (they are the #1 in their space already, but that's only like ~10% market share)\nDiverse team, innovative culture: They strongly encourage and focus on hiring for diversity across all axes, which has led to an incredibly creative and innovative culture\nLots of growth in sight! T hey are making HUGE pivots to grow and take market share in an industry ripe for product-focused development to drive tons of new customers.\nUnique balance of stability and growth: They've been around for 15+ years yet very small and nimble, with plenty of room for new \"startup-like\" initiatives and passionate innovators\nAn AI philosophy that doesn't suck : They are AI-welcoming, but they want solid development fundamentals 1st (Good code and smart architecture will always rule the room).\nRemote 1st, and rooted in that for almost their entire history ... no RTOs happening here. They do remote RIGHT (with many awards to back them) ... This includes remote workflows, async habits, and remote communication patterns that are well established.\nROLE REQUIREMENTS\nThese roles are heavily backend and product-focused . We are seeking engineers who have worked extensively on the server side using Node.js and TypeScript , backed by a proven track record of scaling microservices, executing complex database migrations, and architecting high-throughput, event-driven systems. Ideal candidates bring deep expertise across systems architecture, advanced SQL tuning, ORM management, and clean API design, paired with a strong product mindset focused on delivering core backend business logic that directly drives customer value. They are also looking for people who have done this type of work at scale (i.e., on products with millions of users)\nStrong, recent, production Backend coding execution with a Node / TypeScript focus\nA highly product-focused engineering mentality\nProven depth in working and scaling with high-volume, high-scale products (ideally products with millions of users, using event-driven workflows, and asynchronous systems under heavy load)\nStrong SQL relational database mastery\nDemonstrated ability to lead and mentor other engineers , and clarify requirements during live coding, even when given ambiguous initiatives, without relying on AI tools as a crutch.\nConnection to sports or passion mission-driven companies strongly preferred**\nNOTE: THEY WILL PASS IF ...\nThey have already said \"pass\" to other folks that they felt were not a fit due to them being too heavy into either Platform work and/or being too Heavy on the Front End, not enough Backend experience with Node/Typescript, or working on too small of products: If you feel like any of the below describes YOU, these would NOT be the right roles for you.\nYou are historically heavy into platform engineering work and historically focused on isolated internal infrastructure, distributed systems, and heavy internal tooling rather than shipping tangible end-user features that drive product velocity.\nYou have historically leaned toward the front end, working with React, UI state management, or client-side development\nYou do not have much recent production (at work) backend experience with Node/Typescript\nYou have historically done a lot of work on products with 10s, 100s, or 1000's of daily active users (i.e., you have not worked much on products with 1,000,000+ daily active users)\nLOCATION\n*This role is FULLY REMOTE, but hired candidates must reside in the USA: We have listed the role in a specific city to help mitigate the many thousands of applicants we get who end up being spammers and scammers. NOTE: While the role is remote, my client CANNOT hire residents of Alabama, Alaska, Delaware, the District of Columbia, Hawaii, Iowa, Louisiana, Mississippi, Nebraska, New Mexico, Rhode Island, South Dakota, West Virginia or Utah.\nCOMPENSATION:\nThe minimum salary for this role is $200K, with a budget of up to $220K base salary. If hired, you would also be eligible for a 5% bonus.\nBENEFITS:\nThis client offers a strong benefits package including the following:\n100% employer-paid medical, dental, and vision insurance premiums for both the employee and their entire family .\nUnlimited PTO and paid parental leave for all parents.\n401(k) retirement plan.\n$1,500 annual learning and development stipend.\nHome office setup allowance plus a monthly health and wellness reimbursement stipend.\n$50 annual swag credit after starting.\nTravel covered for all-company meetings and team offsites.\nNEXT STEPS...\nIf you feel that your background and goals align with this role, please drop your resume here. If there is synergy, we will reach out ASAP.\nCheers,\n-Will\nNOTE: This client is unable to offer sponsorship or visa transfers at this time. If you are interested and qualified after reviewing ALL of the requirements carefully, please submit your resume via LinkedIn and do not send any further personal messages. Rest assured, your application WILL be reviewed for a potential fit along with all other resumes via the applicant reviewing portal, and we WILL move forward with the best-fitting candidates. Due to an overwhelming amount of AI-generated spam messages via email and LinkedIn (and from folks who are clearly just not reading the Job Description), personal messages are now being disregarded. Thanks!\n____________________________________________\nWill Wegert — Colorado's #1 Most Bald-est 👨 🦲 #DevRecruiter™ | AKA Colorado's most Reliable, Respected, and Recognized Software Engineering Recruiter.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4481445030": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-27T18:54:56.089348+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "About the role:\nWe’re looking for a software engineer who is also interested in crypto markets and comfortable participating in day trading as part of the role.\nYou’ll work with us to research trading strategies, analyze market data, and build algorithms that can be tested and improved over time. A major part of the work will be studying 10 years or more of historical data where available , identifying patterns, testing hypotheses, and using evidence to evaluate trading ideas.\nThis is one integrated role: you’ll contribute to both the trading work and the software behind it. We’re open to students, recent graduates, and experienced candidates who can show strong technical and analytical skills alongside genuine crypto trading experience.\nWe value practical problem-solving. You should be comfortable finding useful exchanges, APIs, datasets, libraries, open-source projects, and existing tools, then connecting them into a working system. The goal is to build a stable crypto trading algorithm by assembling and improving what already works—not rebuilding every component from scratch.\nWhat you’ll do\nParticipate in crypto market research and day-trading activity.\nAnalyze long-term historical market data, including 10 years or more where reliable data is available.\nCollect, clean, validate, and analyze data from crypto exchanges and other relevant sources.\nUse data analysis and critical thinking to identify patterns, test hypotheses, and assess whether a strategy has evidence behind it.\nStudy price action, market behavior, and trading strategies, and help translate useful ideas into testable rules.\nDevelop Python tools and services for data collection, analysis, and automation.\nWork with exchange APIs, libraries, and other data sources; use scripting or automation where appropriate.\nResearch technical indicators and formulas using reliable references, open-source tools, and AI assistants such as Claude.\nVerify formulas and AI-generated code before using them in analysis or trading systems.\nConnect existing tools and services to fill gaps in the trading workflow.\nBuild and improve backtesting, monitoring, alerting, and execution components.\nTest strategies with historical data and simulated trading, then help evaluate live trading under defined risk limits.\nDocument your methods, assumptions, results, and limitations so the team can make data-informed decisions.\nWhat we’re looking for\nStrong interest in cryptocurrency markets and demonstrable experience buying, selling, or day trading crypto.\nComfort participating in day-trading research and activity as well as software development.\nStrong data analysis and critical analysis skills, with the ability to question assumptions and interpret results carefully.\nWorking knowledge of Python, including writing scripts for data collection, analysis, and automation.\nExperience using APIs, preferably exchange APIs, and handling structured data such as JSON.\nAbility to work with historical and time-series data and to evaluate trading ideas using evidence.\nFamiliarity with appropriate tools for data-driven analysis, such as pandas, NumPy, SQL, notebooks, statistical methods, or visualization tools.\nAbility to research indicators, understand the logic behind them, and translate ideas into code.\nA practical mindset: you look for suitable existing tools and libraries before building a replacement.\nGood communication skills and the ability to explain your reasoning, trading ideas, and technical decisions.\nCuriosity, discipline, and a willingness to learn from experiments that do not produce the expected result.\nHelpful experience\nFamiliarity with crypto exchanges, market-data feeds, order types, and trading dashboards.\nExperience analyzing large datasets, historical price data, or time-series data.\nExposure to backtesting, quantitative analysis, algorithmic trading, or risk management.\nExperience with tools such as Cursor, Claude, or other AI coding assistants.\nContributions to relevant open-source projects or personal trading, data analysis, or software projects.\nWho should apply\nYou do not need a particular degree or a long employment history. Students, recent graduates, self-taught developers, and experienced professionals are all welcome to apply if they can demonstrate relevant skills and trading experience.\nThis role combines hands-on crypto market participation with software engineering and data analysis. If you are interested only in coding and are not comfortable engaging with day-trading activity, this role may not be the right fit.\nHow to apply\nPlease include your résumé or LinkedIn profile.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4481451013": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-27T18:54:56.089348+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Introduction\nA career in IBM Consulting is built on long-term client relationships and close collaboration worldwide. You'll work with leading companies across industries, helping them shape their hybrid cloud and AI journeys. With support from our strategic partners, robust IBM technology, and Red Hat, you'll have the tools to drive meaningful change and accelerate client impact. At IBM Consulting, curiosity fuels success. You'll be encouraged to challenge the norm, explore new ideas, and create innovative solutions that deliver real results. Our culture of growth and empathy focuses on your long-term career development while valuing your unique skills and experiences.\nYour Role And Responsibilities\nAs an Application Developer specializing in SAP ABAP HANA, you will design, develop, and support application solutions with a focus on the HANA version of Advanced Business Application Programming (ABAP). You will work on designing, developing, and re-engineering highly complex application components, integrating software packages, programs, and reusable objects residing on multiple platforms.\nYour Primary Responsibilities Will Include\nDevelop Application Solutions: Design, develop, and support application solutions with a focus on HANA version of ABAP, ensuring seamless integration with existing systems and platforms.\nIntegrate Software Packages: Integrate software packages, programs, and reusable objects residing on multiple platforms, leveraging knowledge of SAP HANA Technical Concept and Architecture.\nRe-engineer Application Components: Re-engineer highly complex application components to optimize performance, scalability, and reliability, utilizing ABAP Development Tools (ADT) and Code Performance Rules and Guidelines for SAP HANA.\nModel Data using HANA Studio: Create data models using HANA Studio, adhering to best practices and ensuring data consistency and integrity.\nConsume HANA Live Models: Consume HANA Live models to deliver real-time insights and analytics, leveraging knowledge of ADBC, Native SQL, and ABAP Core Data Services.\nRequired Technical And Professional Expertise\nExposure to SAP ABAP HANA: Experience working with HANA version of Advanced Business Application Programming (ABAP), including designing, developing, and supporting application solutions.\nKnowledge of SAP HANA Technical Concept and Architecture: Familiarity with SAP HANA Technical Concept and Architecture, including data modeling using HANA Studio and ABAP Development Tools (ADT).\nExperience with Data Modeling: Exposure to data modeling using HANA Studio, adhering to best practices and ensuring data consistency and integrity.\nUnderstanding of Code Performance Rules: Familiarity with Code Performance Rules and Guidelines for SAP HANA, including ADBC, Native SQL, and ABAP Core Data Services.\nIntegration Experience: Experience integrating software packages, programs, and reusable objects residing on multiple platforms.\nPreferred Technical And Professional Experience\nWorking Knowledge of HANA Live: Familiarity with consuming HANA Live models to deliver real-time insights and analytics, leveraging knowledge of ADBC, Native SQL, and ABAP Core Data Services.\nExposure to Database Procedures: Understanding of database procedures, text search, and ALV on HANA, including data base procedures and HANA Live models consumption.\nFamiliarity with ABAP Core Data Services: Knowledge of ABAP Core Data Services, including data modeling and code performance optimization techniques.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4482170870": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-27T18:54:56.089348+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "About FullStack\nFullStack is your AI-native engineering partner, built to turn AI capability into certainty. Most companies can demo AI; few can get it to production and prove what it produced. We close that gap with three capabilities, AI built into your products from the start, elite vetted talent who apply it, and transparent execution that shows value every step of the way. With now over 600 customers in North America, FullStack is one integrated partner for all your AI engineering needs. With FullStack, you move forward with confidence.\nWe’re Most Proud Of\nOffering life-changing career opportunities to talented software professionals across the Americas.\nBuilding highly-skilled software development teams for hundreds of the world’s greatest companies.\nHaving delivered hundreds of successful custom software solutions, which have positively impacted the lives and careers of millions of users.\nOur 4.1-star rating on GlassDoor.\nOur client Net Promoter Score of 68, twice the industry average.\nThe Position\nForward Deployed Engineers sit inside the client’s problem, not next to it. You embed with an enterprise team, find the work that actually warrants AI, architect the system, build it, and make it hold up in the real environment.\nThis is a three-way role: consultant, operator, engineer . You should be as comfortable pressure-testing a business case with a COO or VP of Engineering as you are debugging why an agent’s tool-calling loop degraded after a context change. The people who succeed here can hold a discovery conversation on Monday and ship what they scoped on Thursday.\nOn this track, your edge is application engineering: you make agents real inside the client’s actual systems, workflows, and delivery pipelines.\nWe work with regulated industries and Fortune 500 clients who have AI mandates, real constraints, and low tolerance for demos that don’t hold up.\nHow We Approach The Work\nFDEs are trusted to shape the solution, not only deliver it. Every engagement calls for architect-level judgment:\nReframes the request. Treats “we need an agent for X” as a hypothesis, not a spec.\nDecomposes the problem. Outcome → process → decisions → data → systems → actors → constraints — before choosing technology.\nChooses the intervention. Remove, simplify, traditional software, automation, LLM, RAG, agent, or multi-agent — and defends why.\nOwns the architecture decision. Documents trade-offs (ADRs), sets success metrics, pushes back on scope that won’t deliver value.\nConsultative Discovery\nClients rarely arrive with a fully formed problem, and the FDE’s first contribution is helping them see it clearly. You lead discovery with genuine curiosity, moving the conversation from stated requirements to underlying needs, and you build credibility through the depth of your understanding rather than the breadth of your pitch.\nUncovers business drivers. What outcome matters, what it’s worth, why now, and what happens if nothing changes.\nUncovers personal drivers. What each stakeholder is measured on, what they’re worried about, and what a win looks like for them individually.\nSurfaces constraints early. Security, compliance, data access, budget, skills, politics, timelines — the things that kill projects in month two.\nAligns stakeholders. Spots conflicting goals between business, engineering, and risk, and brings them to a shared definition of success.\nAsks strategic questions. Follows the answer with “why,” “how do you know,” and “what happens today when…” — without interrogating. Clients leave the conversation understanding their own problem better.\nEarns authority through depth. Credibility comes from the quality of the questions and the insight in the playback, not from pitching technology.\nWhat You'll Do\nDiscover. Run workshops and process discovery with business and engineering stakeholders. Separate genuine AI problems from workflow problems wearing an AI costume. Come back with a scoped, defensible point of view.\nStructure the process and the spec. For any business or engineering process being automated, map the current state, decision points, and exceptions, then turn it into specifications that both people and AI systems can execute against reliably.\nArchitect & design. Design agentic systems end to end — orchestration, context and retrieval architecture, tool and MCP integration, guardrails, human-in-the-loop checkpoints, and the boundaries between deterministic and non-deterministic components.\nBuild. Ship working systems — agents, multi-step automations, internal tooling, integration layers. You are hands-on. Prototypes that prove value in weeks, not slideware.\nEngineer the delivery system. Own CI/CD for what you build: build, test, release, environments.\nConsult. Present to and defend decisions in front of CTOs, VPs of Engineering, and business leadership. Quantify impact in their terms. Support pre-sales scoping and proposal work when the deal calls for it.\nWhat We're Looking For\n5+ years of professional software development experience with at least one mainstream production stack (TypeScript/Node.js, Python, Java, C#/.NET, or Go).\n1 - 4 years of professional experience building and shipping LLM-powered and agentic AI systems beyond prototypes or demos.\nAdvanced English is required.\nSuccessful completion of a four-year college degree is required.\nHands-on experience with frontier AI developer tools including Cursor, Claude Code, Gemini CLI, or OpenAI Codex.\nProven experience evaluating current-state environments and defining technical roadmaps.\nDemonstrated experience with APIs, service design, event-driven and distributed systems, and data modeling.\nExperience designing and owning CI/CD pipelines, including build, test, release, environments, and deployment processes.\nStrong understanding of context and specification engineering to produce reliable AI output.\nSolid understanding of enterprise integration patterns, including APIs, webhooks, event streams, iPaaS platforms such as n8n or MuleSoft, and MCP.\nTrack record of leading client-facing discovery calls, asking \"why\" before \"how\" to decompose unstructured business problems.\nSkilled at exercising end-to-end delivery ownership and managing project scope without requiring product manager supervision.\nAbility to work through new and difficult issues and contribute to libraries as needed.\nAbility to create and maintain continuous integration and delivery of applications.\nForensic attention to detail.\nA positive mindset and a can-do attitude.\nExperience working on Agile / Scrum teams.\nMeaningful experience working on large, complex systems.\nAbility to take extreme ownership over your work. Every day is a challenge to ensure you are performing to the expectations you and your team have agreed upon.\nAbility to identify with the goals of FullStack's clients, and dedicate yourself to delivering on the commitments you and your team make to them.\nStrong Plus\nProduction AI operations (Day 2): eval harnesses, observability and tracing, cost and token economics, drift, debugging non-deterministic systems.\nPrompt- and eval-level regression testing running in CI and gating releases.\nDelivery in regulated environments (financial services, healthcare, insurance, manufacturing).\nPre-sales support: discovery calls, SOW and estimate shaping, technical proposal defense.\nProcess mining, operations analysis, or transformation consulting background.\nClient enablement and training — building the client team’s capability, not just the system.\nPrior consulting or agency environment; comfort with ambiguity and multiple accounts.\nWork Authorization Requirements\nApplicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis.\nFullStack will not sponsor applicants for work visas now or in the future.\nWhat We Offer\nCompetitive Salary.\nPaid Time Off (vacation, sick leave, parental leave, holidays).\n100% remote work.\nThe ability to work with leading startups and Fortune 500 companies.\nHealth, dental, and vision insurance.\n401(k) w/ 4% match.\nAmple opportunity for career advancement.\nContinuing education opportunities.\nFullStack is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity, or Veteran status.\nLearn more about our Applicants Privacy Notice.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4482187068": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-27T18:54:56.089348+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "About FullStack\nFullStack is your AI-native engineering partner, built to turn AI capability into certainty. Most companies can demo AI; few can get it to production and prove what it produced. We close that gap with three capabilities, AI built into your products from the start, elite vetted talent who apply it, and transparent execution that shows value every step of the way. With now over 600 customers in North America, FullStack is one integrated partner for all your AI engineering needs. With FullStack, you move forward with confidence.\nWe’re Most Proud Of\nOffering life-changing career opportunities to talented software professionals across the Americas.\nBuilding highly-skilled software development teams for hundreds of the world’s greatest companies.\nHaving delivered hundreds of successful custom software solutions, which have positively impacted the lives and careers of millions of users.\nOur 4.1-star rating on GlassDoor.\nOur client Net Promoter Score of 68, twice the industry average.\nThe Position\nForward Deployed Engineers sit inside the client’s problem, not next to it. You embed with an enterprise team, find the work that actually warrants AI, architect the system, build it, and make it hold up in the real environment.\nThis is a three-way role: consultant, operator, engineer . You should be as comfortable pressure-testing a business case with a COO or VP of Engineering as you are debugging why an agent’s tool-calling loop degraded after a context change. The people who succeed here can hold a discovery conversation on Monday and ship what they scoped on Thursday.\nOn this track, your edge is application engineering: you make agents real inside the client’s actual systems, workflows, and delivery pipelines.\nWe work with regulated industries and Fortune 500 clients who have AI mandates, real constraints, and low tolerance for demos that don’t hold up.\nHow We Approach The Work\nFDEs are trusted to shape the solution, not only deliver it. Every engagement calls for architect-level judgment:\nReframes the request. Treats “we need an agent for X” as a hypothesis, not a spec.\nDecomposes the problem. Outcome → process → decisions → data → systems → actors → constraints — before choosing technology.\nChooses the intervention. Remove, simplify, traditional software, automation, LLM, RAG, agent, or multi-agent — and defends why.\nOwns the architecture decision. Documents trade-offs (ADRs), sets success metrics, pushes back on scope that won’t deliver value.\nConsultative Discovery\nClients rarely arrive with a fully formed problem, and the FDE’s first contribution is helping them see it clearly. You lead discovery with genuine curiosity, moving the conversation from stated requirements to underlying needs, and you build credibility through the depth of your understanding rather than the breadth of your pitch.\nUncovers business drivers. What outcome matters, what it’s worth, why now, and what happens if nothing changes.\nUncovers personal drivers. What each stakeholder is measured on, what they’re worried about, and what a win looks like for them individually.\nSurfaces constraints early. Security, compliance, data access, budget, skills, politics, timelines — the things that kill projects in month two.\nAligns stakeholders. Spots conflicting goals between business, engineering, and risk, and brings them to a shared definition of success.\nAsks strategic questions. Follows the answer with “why,” “how do you know,” and “what happens today when…” — without interrogating. Clients leave the conversation understanding their own problem better.\nEarns authority through depth. Credibility comes from the quality of the questions and the insight in the playback, not from pitching technology.\nWhat You'll Do\nDiscover. Run workshops and process discovery with business and engineering stakeholders. Separate genuine AI problems from workflow problems wearing an AI costume. Come back with a scoped, defensible point of view.\nStructure the process and the spec. For any business or engineering process being automated, map the current state, decision points, and exceptions, then turn it into specifications that both people and AI systems can execute against reliably.\nArchitect & design. Design agentic systems end to end — orchestration, context and retrieval architecture, tool and MCP integration, guardrails, human-in-the-loop checkpoints, and the boundaries between deterministic and non-deterministic components.\nBuild. Ship working systems — agents, multi-step automations, internal tooling, integration layers. You are hands-on. Prototypes that prove value in weeks, not slideware.\nEngineer the delivery system. Own CI/CD for what you build: build, test, release, environments.\nConsult. Present to and defend decisions in front of CTOs, VPs of Engineering, and business leadership. Quantify impact in their terms. Support pre-sales scoping and proposal work when the deal calls for it.\nWhat We're Looking For\n5+ years of professional software development experience with at least one mainstream production stack (TypeScript/Node.js, Python, Java, C#/.NET, or Go).\n1 - 4 years of professional experience building and shipping LLM-powered and agentic AI systems beyond prototypes or demos.\nAdvanced English is required.\nSuccessful completion of a four-year college degree is required.\nHands-on experience with frontier AI developer tools including Cursor, Claude Code, Gemini CLI, or OpenAI Codex.\nProven experience evaluating current-state environments and defining technical roadmaps.\nDemonstrated experience with APIs, service design, event-driven and distributed systems, and data modeling.\nExperience designing and owning CI/CD pipelines, including build, test, release, environments, and deployment processes.\nStrong understanding of context and specification engineering to produce reliable AI output.\nSolid understanding of enterprise integration patterns, including APIs, webhooks, event streams, iPaaS platforms such as n8n or MuleSoft, and MCP.\nTrack record of leading client-facing discovery calls, asking \"why\" before \"how\" to decompose unstructured business problems.\nSkilled at exercising end-to-end delivery ownership and managing project scope without requiring product manager supervision.\nAbility to work through new and difficult issues and contribute to libraries as needed.\nAbility to create and maintain continuous integration and delivery of applications.\nForensic attention to detail.\nA positive mindset and a can-do attitude.\nExperience working on Agile / Scrum teams.\nMeaningful experience working on large, complex systems.\nAbility to take extreme ownership over your work. Every day is a challenge to ensure you are performing to the expectations you and your team have agreed upon.\nAbility to identify with the goals of FullStack's clients, and dedicate yourself to delivering on the commitments you and your team make to them.\nStrong Plus\nProduction AI operations (Day 2): eval harnesses, observability and tracing, cost and token economics, drift, debugging non-deterministic systems.\nPrompt- and eval-level regression testing running in CI and gating releases.\nDelivery in regulated environments (financial services, healthcare, insurance, manufacturing).\nPre-sales support: discovery calls, SOW and estimate shaping, technical proposal defense.\nProcess mining, operations analysis, or transformation consulting background.\nClient enablement and training — building the client team’s capability, not just the system.\nPrior consulting or agency environment; comfort with ambiguity and multiple accounts.\nWork Authorization Requirements\nApplicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis.\nFullStack will not sponsor applicants for work visas now or in the future.\nWhat We Offer\nCompetitive Salary.\nPaid Time Off (vacation, sick leave, parental leave, holidays).\n100% remote work.\nThe ability to work with leading startups and Fortune 500 companies.\nHealth, dental, and vision insurance.\n401(k) w/ 4% match.\nAmple opportunity for career advancement.\nContinuing education opportunities.\nFullStack is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity, or Veteran status.\nLearn more about our Applicants Privacy Notice.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4482694167": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-27T18:54:56.089348+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "IMPORTANT: after you apply, please check your email. We send you a link to complete your application — it is not considered until that last step is done. If you do not see it, check your spam folder.\nThis is a fully remote position , open to candidates based in 55 countries, including United States, United Kingdom, Canada, Germany, India, France, Netherlands, Singapore.\nPay: $180,000–$250,000/yr\nJob Title: Software Engineer, New Grad\nJob Type: Full-time\nLocation : Remote\nThe Role\nThis is a fullstack software engineering role designed for recent graduates and early-career engineers looking to accelerate their growth by building production systems. You'll contribute to — and grow into owning — core internal platform capabilities and product features end-to-end.\nYou'll work across internal tools, services, workflows, and AI-powered products that support our engineering, operations, and recruiting platforms. As you grow, you'll take increasing ownership of critical systems while collaborating closely with experienced engineers.\nWhat You'll Own\nContribute to the design and development of end-to-end fullstack systems powering critical internal workflows and platform capabilities.\nBuild clean, maintainable backend services and APIs while learning scalable engineering best practices.\nDevelop high-quality frontend interfaces used by internal teams and end users.\nParticipate in data modeling and database optimization efforts, including schema design and query performance.\nCollaborate with product, operations, and design teams to translate ideas into reliable, production-ready features.\nImprove engineering quality through code reviews, testing, documentation, and continuous improvement.\nHelp troubleshoot production issues while learning how to build resilient, observable systems.\nDevelop sound engineering judgment by making thoughtful tradeoffs between speed, scalability, and maintainability.\nWhat We're Looking For\nBachelor's degree in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Software Engineering, or a related field (recent graduate or graduating soon).\nInternship, co-op, research, or meaningful personal/project experience building software applications.\nStrong fundamentals in JavaScript and/or TypeScript.\nFamiliarity with frontend development using React or similar frameworks.\nFamiliarity with backend development using Node.js (NestJS is a plus).\nUnderstanding of relational databases such as PostgreSQL and core data modeling principles.\nFamiliarity with RESTful APIs and how distributed applications communicate.\nExposure to Git and modern software development workflows.\nStrong problem-solving skills, curiosity, attention to detail, and a growth mindset.\nExcited to learn quickly and contribute in a fast-moving engineering environment.\nPreferred\nInternship or professional software engineering experience.\nExposure to cloud platforms such as AWS, GCP, or Azure.\nFamiliarity with CI/CD, deployment pipelines, or DevOps fundamentals.\nExposure to modern architectures such as microservices, serverless, or event-driven systems.\nInterest in AI-powered products, workflow automation, or data-intensive applications.\nExperience contributing to team projects, hackathons, open-source software, or startup environments.\nCompensation & Benefits Notice\nThe national pay range for this full-time position is base salary of $110,000 –$150,000 USD. All employees are eligible for equity compensation, and employees may also receive performance-based bonuses, dependent on role and subject to company policies. The company provides a comprehensive benefits package, including up to 100% reimbursement for health-insurance premiums, paid time off, a 401(K) plan with a company match, and additional benefits designed to support a high-performing, remote-first workforce.\nthe company is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy, sexual orientation, or gender identity), national origin, age, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable local laws, regulations and ordinances. If you need assistance and/or a reasonable accommodation during the application process, reach out to us by replying to our email.\nOur hiring process utilizes artificial intelligence tools to assist in candidate screening and assessment. Our AI tools are designed to complement, not replace, human decision-making.\nDisclaimer\nThe information contained in this job posting, including but not limited to role responsibilities, qualifications, compensation, and benefits, is provided for informational purposes only and does not constitute a binding offer of employment. the company reserves the right to amend, modify, or withdraw any portion of this posting at its sole discretion and without prior notice. All employment decisions are made in accordance with applicable laws and regulations.\nHow To Apply\nApply here with your profile. We will then email you a link to complete your application on the hiring platform — your application is only considered once that final step is done.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4482701648": {
