      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4482707156": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-27T18:54:56.089348+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Devsinc is looking for motivated AI/ML Associates to join our team and contribute to the development of innovative Artificial Intelligence and Machine Learning solutions. This role offers an opportunity to work on real-world projects, enhance technical expertise, and grow in a collaborative, technology-driven environment.\nRequirements\nDevelop, train, test, and optimize machine learning models for real-world applications.\nAssist in designing and implementing AI-powered solutions using machine learning and deep learning techniques.\nCollect, clean, preprocess, and analyze structured and unstructured datasets.\nWork with libraries such as NumPy, Pandas, Scikit-learn, TensorFlow, or PyTorch.\nExplore and implement Generative AI solutions using Large Language Models (LLMs), APIs, and prompt engineering.\nEvaluate model performance using appropriate metrics and improve accuracy and efficiency.\nCollaborate with software engineers and cross-functional teams to integrate AI/ML models into applications.\nMaintain technical documentation and follow best practices for code quality, testing, and version control.\nStay updated with emerging AI/ML technologies, tools, and industry trends.\nQualification:\nBachelor's degree in Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, Data Science, Software Engineering, or a related field.\n6 months to 1 year of practical experience in AI/ML development through professional work, internships, or relevant projects.\nStrong programming fundamentals and a basic understanding of machine learning concepts.\nA portfolio of relevant projects or practical implementations is a plus.\nRequired Skills:\nProficiency in Python programming.\nWorking knowledge of NumPy, Pandas, and Scikit-learn.\nUnderstanding of supervised and unsupervised learning algorithms.\nBasic knowledge of deep learning concepts and frameworks such as TensorFlow or PyTorch.\nFamiliarity with data preprocessing, feature engineering, and model evaluation techniques.\nBasic understanding of REST APIs, Git, and model deployment.\nFamiliarity with Generative AI, LLMs, and prompt engineering is an advantage.\nStrong analytical, problem-solving, and communication skills.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4482709479": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-27T18:54:56.089348+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "About Brkthru:\nBrkthru was founded with a client-centric philosophy in an industry where service is often overlooked. Our mission is to be the preferred partner of local advertisers and agencies, creating and managing successful paid digital media campaigns for local, state, regional and national brands in nearly every B2C and B2B vertical and industry. Our campaigns reach customers on digital devices such as smartphones, tablets, computers and digital TV.\nWe are guided by our core values and we center them in the hiring process and our workday to build teams that exemplify Positive Attitude, Caring, Contribution, Communication, and Trust.\nWhy Brkthru?\nBrkthru is the leading digital media solutions provider to mid-market agencies and brands. Our trading works in 20+ different digital media platforms, but our client-first philosophy sets us apart, consistently earning us a 90% client satisfaction rating, and equally impressive client retention is proof. We are growing quickly, ranking for the fifth year in-a-row to the Inc. 5000 Fastest Growing Private Companies in America.\nThe Opportunity\nThis role is ideal for someone who enjoys building production software from front to back. You'll spend your time developing new features, maintaining existing systems, designing APIs, solving complex engineering problems, and partnering closely with teammates to deliver reliable software.\nIn the near term, you'll help ensure a smooth transition of ownership for BRAVO while learning the platform from our current engineer. Longer term, you'll help modernize the platform and contribute to Brkthru's broader investments in automation, AI, and internal tooling.\nResponsibilities:\nApplication Development\nDesign, build, test, and deploy production features across the BRAVO platform.\nDevelop full-stack applications spanning React, Node.js, APIs, and PostgreSQL.\nWrite clean, maintainable, and well-tested code.\nDebug production issues and improve system reliability.\nPlatform Ownership\nBecome a primary technical owner of BRAVO.\nImprove platform performance, scalability, and maintainability.\nIdentify technical debt and recommend architectural improvements.\nContribute to long-term platform modernization.\nEngineering Collaboration\nPartner with Product, Engineering, and business stakeholders to translate requirements into technical solutions.\nParticipate in code reviews and technical design discussions.\nHelp maintain development standards and engineering best practices.\nCloud & Infrastructure\nBuild and maintain services hosted within AWS.\nWork with Docker, CI/CD pipelines, infrastructure, and deployment automation.\nMonitor application health and production environments.\nExperience\n6+ years of professional software engineering experience.\nStrong experience with Node.js and TypeScript.\nExperience building React applications.\nStrong SQL and PostgreSQL skills.\nExperience designing and consuming REST APIs.\nExperience working in AWS cloud environments.\nFamiliarity with CI/CD pipelines and Git workflows.\nComfortable debugging production applications.\nTech Stack:\nFrontend: React 19, TypeScript, Vite, TanStack Query, Zustand, Tailwind CSS\nBackend: Node.js, Express, Bun, TRPC, Database, PostgreSQL\nInfrastructure: AWS (ECS, RDS, S3, CloudFront), Docker, Terraform, GitHub Actions\nTesting: Jest, Playwright\nProject & Collaboration Skills\nExperience managing technical work within Jira or similar tools\nAbility to manage multiple concurrent projects with minimal oversight\nStrong written and verbal communication skills\nTravel/Onsite Requirements:\nBrkthru operates as a remote-first company with occasional mandatory travel for training and offsites, provided with advance notice. We uphold the expectation that all team members maintain a dedicated and reliable workspace, free from distractions, to ensure optimal productivity.\nThis role requires travel 2-3 times per year for our offsites. Travel instances are typically 3-5 days at a time.\nBenefits\nThis is a full-time, exempt position\nMedical/ Dental/ Vision/ HSA and FSA/ Long Term Disability/ Life and AD&D/ and more…\nCompany paid Short Term Disability\n401k Retirement plan with company match\nPizza Fridays and Hub Hangouts\nReimbursement of Home Office Expenses\nA generous number of Holidays, PTO, and summer Fridays\nBrkthru Hiring and AI Usage\nBrkthru welcomes candidates to use AI tools for proofreading or strengthening their resume, but submitting AI-generated cover letters, resumes, or work samples that do not accurately represent a candidate’s skills will be considered a red flag. The use of AI-powered 'whispering bots' or real-time answer-generation apps during live interviews is strictly prohibited.\nAll candidate applications are reviewed by a human. Brkthru may use artificial intelligence (AI) or automated tools to assist in the evaluation of applications, assessment scoring, and interview analysis or notetaking; however, all hiring decisions are made by people.\nBrkthru EEO Statement\nWe’re proud to be an Equal Opportunity Employer and committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, creed, sex, sexual orientation, gender, gender identity or expression, pregnancy (including childbirth, lactation, and related conditions), national origin or ancestry, ethnicity, age, family status, marital status, veteran or military status, the presence of a medical condition or physical or mental disability, height, weight, misdemeanor arrest record, genetic information, citizenship, hair (including texture or protective hairstyle), or any other characteristic protected by applicable law, and encourage all applicants to apply.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4482718175": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-27T18:54:56.089348+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "About Contour\nContour Software has grown from a dozen people to over 2,000 staff across 3 cities, in less than 14 years.\nAs a subsidiary of Constellation Software Inc., we are proud to be part of a global enterprise software conglomerate that has grown to become one of the top 10 software companies in the world, with employees and customers in 100+ countries. With a broad-based and ever-growing portfolio of market-leading, vertical-market enterprise solutions covering more than 100 industry domains in predominantly mature markets, CSI's recipe creates the perfect environment for professionals to build fulfilling, long-term careers.\nWhat started as an R&D & Accounting back-office, has progressed into a full-service Global Centre serving all functions and departments, at the divisional as well as operating group/corporate level. Today Contour employees, located in Karachi, Lahore & Islamabad, are serving CSI divisions located in time zones spanning the globe, from Sydney to Vancouver. With the global growth of Constellation as the wind in our sails, we are only just getting started!\nThe Division\nJonas Premier Construction - a division of Constellation Software Inc. – is the market-leading cloud-based integrated construction management solution, for mid-sized General Contractors, Design Builders and Land Developers. Constellation companies are leading developers of technology solutions for vertical markets in North America, Europe and Australia. Jonas Software is the valued technology partner of over 8000 customers worldwide in 15 countries. Jonas is headquartered in Canada and also operates offices in the United States, the United Kingdom, and the Caribbean.\nThe Position\nWe are looking for Trainee Software Developers to join one of our R&D teams. The selected candidates will be trained for 3 to 3.5 months to become good developers capable of working on enterprise-level applications. After the end of the internship period, there is a good possibility of full-time employment based on satisfactory performance during the internship.\nThe chosen individuals will work out of the Contour Software Lahore resource center office, as an extension of the division-based R&D department.\nRequired Qualifications & Skills\nBS/MS in Computer Science or related field.\nStrong understanding of object-oriented programming principles.\nGood programming concepts and knowledge of .NET programming\nExposure to Generative AI, LLMs, RAG, Prompt Engineering, or AI-powered application development.\nStrong competencies in data structures, algorithms, and software design.\nStrong relational database concepts with SQL queries.\nGood level of knowledge of REST APIs.\nExperience and knowledge of Git.\nA quick learner, with attention to detail, and a commitment to meet deadlines.\nKnowledge of professional software engineering practices\nGood programming concepts and knowledge of frontend programming with JavaScript, AngularJS/Angular.\nGood communication skills in English.\nDisclaimer: At Contour, we attribute our success to the unique contributions of our diverse staff. We’re committed to fostering a culture of respect that thrives on the varied perspectives and experiences of all individuals we recruit, employ, promote, and compensate. Since day one, we’ve adhered to a policy that champions a work environment honoring the worth and dignity of each person while being free from all forms of employment discrimination.\nIn our continuous effort to promote inclusivity, we extend our commitment to individuals with special needs by providing reasonable accommodations. We actively encourage qualified individuals with special needs to apply for the various openings within our company. Should you require assistance in completing the application process or have any inquiries regarding special facilities, please do not hesitate to contact our HR team. Your unique talents and abilities are welcomed and valued here.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4482724038": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-27T18:54:56.089348+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "This position is fully remote / work from home.\nSalary: $104,000 - 114,000/year\nWe are seeking a versatile Software Engineer with 3+ years of experience to join our engineering team. In this role, you will design, build, and maintain robust web applications across our full tech stack, contributing to modernizing and scaling our core application infrastructure. Our core tech stack centers on Python (FastAPI) on the backend, Vue.js on the frontend, and PostgreSQL for data management. You will work across the stack to build high-performance REST APIs, responsive user interfaces, and efficient database architectures.\nKey Responsibilities\nBuild, test, and maintain backend APIs using FastAPI and modern, interactive user interfaces using Vue.js.\nDesign, optimize, and maintain relational schemas, complex queries, and migrations in PostgreSQL.\nOptimize application performance, refactor legacy components, and ensure high availability, security, and scalability across the stack.\nDesign secure, well-documented RESTful APIs and handle data pipeline or microservice integrations.\nWrite clean, maintainable, and well-tested code (unit and integration testing). Follow secure coding best practices required for federal/government systems.\nPartner with DevOps engineers, UI/UX designers, and product managers in an Agile development environment.\nRequired Qualifications\n3+ years of professional software engineering experience working with full-stack web applications.\nStrong proficiency in Python with hands-on experience using FastAPI (or comparable modern Python web frameworks like Flask or Django).\nSolid proficiency with Vue.js (Vue 2/3, Options/Composition API) and modern frontend tooling (HTML5, CSS3, JavaScript/TypeScript).\nStrong hands-on experience with PostgreSQL, including schema design, query optimization, and ORMs (e.g., SQLAlchemy).\nSolid understanding of RESTful API design, Git version control, asynchronous programming in Python, and software design patterns.\nMust be eligible to successfully undergo a background investigation to obtain and maintain a Public Trust clearance.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4482932734": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-27T18:54:56.089348+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "This position is listed on behalf of a partner company, which manages all applications and next steps. Our partner is looking for an Associate Software Engineer based in the United States.\nWe are seeking a motivated Associate Software Engineer to contribute to the development, testing, and continuous improvement of innovative software solutions in the healthcare technology sector. In this role, you will collaborate with experienced engineers and cross-functional teams to build reliable, scalable, and maintainable applications that support better healthcare outcomes. You will work with modern development practices and AI-assisted engineering tools to streamline workflows, improve code quality, and accelerate software delivery. The position also offers opportunities to explore data platforms, machine learning pipelines, and generative AI technologies while strengthening your technical expertise. You will contribute to architectural discussions, quality assurance, documentation, and reusable engineering practices within a collaborative and supportive environment. This is an excellent opportunity for an early-career engineer eager to grow professionally while making a meaningful impact through technology.\nAccountabilities\nSoftware Development: Collaborate with engineering teams to design, develop, test, and maintain software applications. Write clean, efficient, secure, and maintainable code that follows established development standards and best practices.\nFeature Development and Enhancement: Contribute to the implementation of new features, application improvements, and technical solutions aligned with business and project requirements.\nCode Reviews and Quality Assurance: Participate in peer code reviews, identify potential improvements, and help ensure code quality, consistency, reliability, and compliance with engineering standards.\nTroubleshooting and Debugging: Investigate software defects, diagnose technical issues, implement corrective solutions, and support ongoing application maintenance.\nTesting and Validation: Develop and execute tests to validate application functionality, reliability, and performance, ensuring solutions meet defined quality requirements.\nCross-Functional Collaboration: Work closely with engineers and other stakeholders to understand requirements, clarify technical specifications, and deliver effective software solutions.\nAI-Assisted Engineering: Apply AI-powered development tools throughout the software delivery lifecycle, including requirements analysis, coding, testing, debugging, documentation, and operational monitoring.\nArchitecture and Solution Design: Use AI-assisted workflows to explore design alternatives, evaluate architectural approaches, improve existing systems, and prepare technical design artifacts for review.\nAI Output Validation: Assess AI-generated code and other technical outputs for correctness, security, maintainability, regulatory compliance, and alignment with business needs. Help review AI-assisted work produced by other engineers.\nData Platform Development: Contribute to the design and maintenance of data platforms and governed datasets that support analytics, machine learning, and generative AI applications.\nReusable Engineering Practices: Develop and share reusable prompts, AI agents, engineering playbooks, development workflows, and automation patterns that improve productivity across the engineering organization.\nDocumentation and Continuous Improvement: Maintain clear technical documentation, stay informed about emerging technologies, and recommend improvements to engineering tools, processes, and delivery practices.\nResponsible AI and Compliance: Ensure that AI-assisted development activities follow organizational policies and applicable requirements for intellectual property, information security, privacy, protected health information (PHI), and responsible AI use.\nRequirements\nEducation: Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or a related technical discipline.\nProgramming Skills: Proficiency in at least one programming language, such as C# or Python, with the ability to write readable, efficient, and maintainable code.\nSoftware Development Fundamentals: Basic understanding of software engineering principles, application development lifecycles, testing methodologies, debugging techniques, and coding best practices.\nVersion Control: Familiarity with Git or comparable version control systems for managing code changes and collaborating with other developers.\nAgile Methodologies: Understanding of software development methodologies such as Agile and Scrum, including collaborative planning, iterative delivery, and continuous improvement.\nProblem-Solving Skills: Strong analytical thinking, attention to detail, and the ability to investigate technical issues and develop practical solutions.\nCommunication and Collaboration: Good written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to work effectively within a team, receive feedback, and contribute to shared engineering objectives.\nAdaptability and Learning: Willingness to learn new technologies, explore emerging engineering practices, and continuously improve technical capabilities.\nAI-Assisted Development Experience: Familiarity with AI-powered coding tools and a demonstrated ability to use them effectively in software development is preferred. Relevant platforms may include GitHub Copilot, Cursor, Claude Code, or similar solutions.\nPrompt Engineering and AI Delivery: Strong prompt-writing skills and experience applying AI-assisted techniques to coding, testing, debugging, and other stages of software delivery are desirable.\nData and AI Technologies: Exposure to machine learning data pipelines, vector search, document processing, data preparation, or generative AI workloads is an advantage.\nData Governance: Working knowledge of data governance, data lineage, data quality, and observability practices supporting reliable AI-enabled solutions is preferred.\nSecurity and Responsible AI: Understanding of secure software development, privacy protection, intellectual property safeguards, and responsible AI principles, particularly in environments handling sensitive healthcare information.\nRemote Work Readiness: Ability to work remotely with a reliable high-speed internet connection exceeding 10 Mbps and the technical setup required to perform the role effectively.\nBenefits\nComprehensive Benefits Package: Access to a range of employee benefits, including health insurance, for eligible employees.\nRemote Work Environment: Work-from-home flexibility designed to support productivity and work-life balance.\nWork-Life Balance: A workplace culture that values employee wellbeing, flexibility, and autonomy.\nProfessional Development: Opportunities to expand technical skills, learn emerging technologies, and develop expertise in software engineering and AI-assisted development.\nInnovative Technology Exposure: Hands-on experience with AI-powered engineering tools, machine learning data platforms, and generative AI development practices.\nCollaborative Culture: Opportunities to work alongside engineers and cross-functional colleagues in an environment that values inclusion, teamwork, and continuous learning.\nMeaningful Impact: The opportunity to contribute to technology solutions that support healthcare organizations and help improve outcomes for people with complex medical needs.\nInclusive Workplace: A commitment to equal employment opportunities, accessibility, and respect for diverse backgrounds and perspectives.\nCompensation: Salary details were not specified in the available job posting. Compensation is determined according to the position's requirements, the selected candidate's skills, and relevant professional experience.\nHow Jobgether Works\nWe use an AI-powered matching process to ensure your application is reviewed quickly, objectively, and fairly against the role's core requirements. Our system identifies the top-fitting candidates, and this shortlist is then shared directly with the hiring company. The final decision and next steps (interviews, assessments) are managed by their internal team.\nWe appreciate your interest and wish you the best!\nWhy Apply Through Jobgether?\nData Privacy Notice: By submitting your application, you acknowledge that Jobgether will process your personal data to evaluate your candidacy and share relevant information with the hiring employer. This processing is based on legitimate interest and pre-contractual measures under applicable data protection laws (including GDPR). You may exercise your rights (access, rectification, erasure, objection) at any time.\nWe may use artificial intelligence (AI) tools to support parts of the hiring process, such as reviewing applications, analyzing resumes, or assessing responses and identifying potential inconsistencies or verification signals in application materials based on available information. These tools assist our recruitment team but do not replace human judgment. Final hiring decisions are ultimately made by humans. If you would like more information about how your data is processed, please contact us.",
