        "payload": {
          "description": "This is a Fully Remote Job\nAbout Our Client:\nThis organization operates in the software engineering sector, focusing on developing internal tools, services, workflows, and AI-powered products that support engineering, operations, and recruiting platforms. It addresses the challenge of creating scalable, reliable software systems that enhance internal processes and productivity. The company is positioned to impact the engineering and operational efficiency through innovative platform capabilities.\nAbout the Opportunity:\nThe SOFTWARE ENGINEER, NEW GRAD role is designed for recent graduates and early-career engineers aiming to accelerate their professional growth by building production software systems. This position involves contributing to and eventually owning core internal platform capabilities and product features. The role is critical in supporting internal workflows and platforms, ensuring the delivery of reliable, maintainable, and scalable software solutions.\nResponsibilities:\nContribute to the design and development of end-to-end fullstack systems supporting critical internal workflows and platforms.\nBuild maintainable backend services and APIs following scalable engineering practices.\nDevelop high-quality frontend interfaces for internal teams and end users.\nParticipate in data modeling and database optimization, including schema design and query performance.\nCollaborate with product, operations, and design teams to translate concepts into production-ready features.\nImprove engineering quality through code reviews, testing, documentation, and continuous improvements.\nAssist in troubleshooting production issues to build resilient and observable systems.\nDevelop engineering judgment to balance speed, scalability, and maintainability.\nRequirements:\nBachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Software Engineering, or related field (recent graduate or soon to graduate).\nExperience through internships, co-ops, research, or personal projects in software application development.\nStrong fundamentals in JavaScript and/or TypeScript.\nFamiliarity with frontend development using React or similar frameworks.\nFamiliarity with backend development using Node.js (NestJS is a plus).\nUnderstanding of relational databases such as PostgreSQL and data modeling principles.\nKnowledge of RESTful APIs and distributed application communication.\nExposure to Git and modern software development workflows.\nStrong problem-solving skills, curiosity, attention to detail, and a growth mindset.\nMotivation to learn quickly and contribute in a fast-paced engineering environment.\nPreferred:\nInternship or professional software engineering experience.\nExposure to cloud platforms like AWS, GCP, or Azure.\nFamiliarity with CI/CD, deployment pipelines, or DevOps fundamentals.\nExposure to modern architectures such as microservices, serverless, or event-driven systems.\nInterest in AI-powered products, workflow automation, or data-intensive applications.\nExperience contributing to team projects, hackathons, open-source software, or startup environments.\nPay Range and Compensation Package:\nThe pay range and compensation package for this role will be determined based on the candidate's experience, skills, and other relevant factors.\nEqual Opportunity Statement:\nOur client is an equal opportunity employer. They celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, or national origin.\nNote:\nTalentHop is a recruitment partner of this role. Please note that all employment decisions, including candidate assessment, interviews, hiring, compensation, and employment terms, are made exclusively by the hiring employer."
        }
