      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4484033358": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-27T18:04:35.875414+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "<strong><strong>About Kodifly<br><br></strong></strong>Kodifly is an AI-first spatial intelligence company transforming infrastructure monitoring and management. Headquartered in Hong Kong Science Park, with an expanded presence in Pakistan and ongoing expansion into the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia, we are backed by HKAI Lab and the Nvidia Inception program. Our expertise spans 3D point cloud processing, digital twin creation, and LiDAR technology. We develop intelligent infrastructure solutions that enable cities and enterprises to operate with greater efficiency and insight. By integrating AI-powered analytics, digital twins, and real-time spatial intelligence, we help our partners streamline asset inspections, elevate quality assurance, and enhance safety throughout the entire infrastructure lifecycle.<br><br><strong><strong>The Kodifly Graduate Program 2027<br><br></strong></strong>Islamabad (NSTP, NUST)<br><br><ul><li> Full-time<br><br></li></ul>The Kodifly Graduate Program is our full-time entry route for fresh graduates from leading universities in Pakistan. From day one you join a working team, take on live projects for international clients and learn directly from our engineers and leadership.<br><br><strong><strong>Who This Is For<br><br></strong></strong><ul><li>Final-year students graduating in 2027</li><li>2026 graduates with less than 1 year of full-time work experience</li><li>Degree in computer science, engineering, design or a related field (each track below lists what fits)</li><li>Available to work full-time, on-site at our Islamabad office at NSTP, NUST<br><br></li></ul><strong>Why Apply Now<br><br></strong><ul><li>Secure your job early, before you graduate. </li><li>One application, three tracks. Choose the track that fits you in the application form. <br><br></li></ul><strong>Track 1: AI Software Engineer<br><br></strong>You build the AI software behind SpatialSense. You are a software engineer first: you build the backend, APIs, data pipelines and product features our clients use every day, and you bring AI into the product where it adds real value.<br><br><strong><strong>Key Responsibilities<br><br></strong></strong><ul><li>Design, build and maintain backend services, APIs and product features for SpatialSense</li><li>Build data pipelines that process LiDAR point clouds, BIM models, 360° images and video at scale</li><li>Integrate AI and computer vision models into production systems, and make them reliable, fast and scalable</li><li>Write clean, tested, well-documented code, and take part in code reviews</li><li>Deploy and run services on the cloud, and help improve our development and release workflow</li><li>Work with product, design and AI teams to ship features end to end<br><br></li></ul><strong><strong>Qualifications<br><br></strong></strong><ul><li>Degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, Computer Engineering or a related field</li><li>Strong Python programming</li><li>Solid fundamentals in data structures, algorithms, databases (SQL) and Git</li><li>Understanding of how web services and REST APIs work</li><li>Exposure to ML or computer vision through coursework, a final-year project or side projects</li><li>A GitHub, final-year project or portfolio that shows real code you have written<br><br></li></ul><strong>Nice to have:</strong> Django or another backend framework, OpenCV, cloud platforms (AWS or GCP), Docker, JavaScript/TypeScript or React, working with BIM or 360° imagery, experience deploying ML models or using LLM APIs, hackathon or competitive programming results<br><br><strong><strong>Track 2: Product Designer<br><br></strong></strong>You design SpatialSense so it is easy to use and easy to sell, and you work hand in hand with engineers to ship what you design.<br><br><strong><strong>Key Responsibilities<br><br></strong></strong><ul><li>Run user research to understand workflows and pain points</li><li>Create wireframes, user flows and prototypes in Figma</li><li>Design clean, consistent interfaces using our design system</li><li>Design with a commercial eye: make the product look and position well for sales, and support demos and pitches</li><li>Work with engineers through agile sprints so designs are built as intended<br><br></li></ul><strong><strong>Qualifications<br><br></strong></strong><ul><li>Degree in Design, HCI, Computer Science or a related field</li><li>Strong Figma skills</li><li>A portfolio of university, internship or personal projects (required)</li><li>Understanding of design systems and systems thinking</li><li>Self-motivated, with a go-getter attitude<br><br></li></ul><strong>Nice to have:</strong> Adobe Creative Suite, AI design tools, interest in B2B or SaaS products.<br><br><strong><strong>Track 3: Technical Project Associate<br><br></strong></strong>You help drive our projects from kickoff to delivery, keeping engineering, clients and timelines aligned.<br><br><strong><strong>Key Responsibilities<br><br></strong></strong><ul><li>Support projects from initiation to completion against scope, timeline and budget</li><li>Work with internal teams and clients to define requirements and deliverables</li><li>Track milestones, schedules and risks, and flag issues early</li><li>Prepare technical proposals, implementation plans, test plans, reports and presentations</li><li>Help improve how we run projects<br><br></li></ul><strong><strong>Qualifications<br><br></strong></strong><ul><li>Degree in Engineering, Computer Science, Project Management or a related field</li><li>Strong organization and multitasking</li><li>Excellent communication in English</li><li>Familiarity with Gantt charts, work breakdown structures and workflow diagrams</li><li>Basic knowledge of Agile and Scrum<br><br></li></ul><strong>Nice to have:</strong> knowledge of LiDAR or digital twins, an internship in a tech or software environment.<br><br><strong>We Offer<br><br></strong><ul><li>Opportunity to work with state-of-the-art technology in a rapidly evolving field</li><li>Real ownership from day one, working with an international team across Hong Kong and Pakistan</li><li>A collaborative environment where innovation is encouraged and rewarded</li><li>Competitive salary</li><li>Fast-track internal growth and promotions for top performers<br><br></li></ul><strong><strong>Join Us at Kodifly<br><br></strong></strong>If you are graduating soon and want to start your career building technology that keeps real infrastructure safe, we want to hear from you. Apply on this page, choose your track, and fill out the form. 🚀<br><br>"
        }
      },
