      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4484073570": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-27T18:04:35.875414+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "About the Company\nUSAble Life is an insurance company committed to making a meaningful difference in the lives of its customers, employees, and communities. The company promotes diversity, equity, and inclusion, encouraging employees to contribute their perspectives and talents. Recognized as a Best Place to Work in Arkansas, Florida, and Hawaii, USAble Life supports professional development, career advancement, and a collaborative workplace culture.\nAbout the Role\nUSAble Life is seeking Web Developers at the Developer I and Developer II levels to analyze, develop, implement, maintain, and test software applications that support the company's systems and business operations. The role involves translating business requirements into technical solutions, collaborating with Business Analysts and Lead Developers, supporting quality assurance and deployments, and maintaining software quality throughout the development lifecycle.\nThe ideal candidate has a strong foundation in programming, object-oriented concepts, database queries, secure coding, and software testing. Developer II candidates must also meet the additional experience requirements specified for that level. This position may involve projects of varying sizes with system-wide impact and participation in a rotating on-call schedule that includes night support.\nKey Responsibilities\nWork with Business Analysts and Lead Developers to identify and document business requirements related to integration processes.\nAnalyze defined system specifications and translate requirements into workable software solutions.\nDevelop, implement, maintain, and test software applications supporting company systems.\nRecommend practical solutions to processing problems and application issues.\nSupport quality assurance activities, software testing, and deployment processes.\nParticipate in code reviews to provide feedback, learn development best practices, and ensure consistency across applications.\nAssist with application planning, design, development, and deployment.\nCommunicate work progress and project status proactively to the development team and project stakeholders.\nReview code to ensure compliance with development standards, coding conventions, and consistency requirements.\nApply secure coding practices, object-oriented programming principles, and established design patterns.\nPerform other related duties and responsibilities as assigned.\nParticipate in rotating on-call responsibilities, including providing support during nighttime hours.\nRequired Qualifications\nBachelor's degree in Computer Science, Information Systems, or a related field, or a curriculum or experience aligned with the required skills.\nAt least 1 year of IT experience for Developer I.\nAt least 2 years of IT experience for Developer II.\nEquivalent military experience may satisfy the education and experience requirement stated for Developer I.\nExperience with open-source tools such as log4net, NUnit, and NHibernate.\nExperience using version control systems such as Git.\nExperience writing SQL queries on database platforms such as Microsoft SQL Server, MySQL, or Oracle.\nExperience with software development or release tracking tools such as Jira or Targetprocess.\nStrong understanding of programming concepts, object-oriented programming, secure coding practices, and design patterns.\nStrong analytical and problem-solving skills.\nAbility to work effectively in a team environment.\nKeen attention to detail and a commitment to software quality.\nStrong communication and interpersonal skills.\nAbility to manage assigned tasks and deliver work within established timelines.\nUnderstanding of software testing tools, unit testing, integration testing, test scripting, and testing methodologies.\nPreferred Qualifications\nFor Developer I: Curriculum or coursework focused on SQL and Microsoft .NET.\nFor Developer I: At least 2 years of IT experience.\nFor Developer I: IT-related experience in the health insurance industry.\nFor Developer II: Experience with continuous integration and continuous delivery (CI/CD) pipelines.\nFor Developer II: At least 3 years of IT experience.\nSalary and Benefits\nDeveloper I anticipated annual salary range: $63,000–$75,000.\nDeveloper II anticipated annual salary range: $79,000–$95,000.\nAnnual incentive plan eligibility based on company and individual performance.\nMedical, dental, and vision benefits.\nPaid time off provided at the date of hire.\n11 paid holidays.\n401(k) plan with an employer match of up to 6%, fully vested from the first day.\nRemote work opportunities with company-provided equipment.\nTuition reimbursement.\nEmployee Assistance Program (EAP).\nInclusion Council and Employee Resource Groups.\nRecharge Days and Volunteer Time Off.\nOpportunities for professional development and career advancement.\nLocation and Work Arrangement\nUSAble Life offers remote work opportunities and provides company equipment for eligible arrangements. The specific work arrangement for this position should be confirmed with the employer.\nThe role includes rotating on-call duties, which may require nighttime support.\nEqual Employment Opportunity\nUSAble Life is an equal opportunity employer. Applicants are entitled to consideration under applicable federal employment laws and protections. The company values diversity, equity, and inclusion and is committed to providing opportunities for employees to contribute and grow."
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4484202093": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-27T18:04:35.875414+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "<strong>Software Quality Engineer (AI-Augmented Testing &amp; Critical Analysis)Job Description<br><br></strong><ul><li>Analyze business requirements, user stories, and acceptance criteria to identify gaps, ambiguities, contradictions, and potential risks.</li><li>Perform functional, exploratory, regression, integration, end-to-end, API, and edge-case testing.</li><li>Use AI for test scenarios, test data, scripts, log summaries, and root-cause analysis, while catching hallucinations and weak output.</li><li>Investigate defects using browser developer tools, application logs, API responses, database records, and monitoring tools.</li><li>Test REST APIs, validate request/response contracts, verify authorization and error handling, and use SQL to ensure data integrity.</li><li>Perform load and performance testing using JMeter and Locust.</li><li>Develop and maintain automated tests using Selenium, Python, or JavaScript.</li><li>Validate fixes, assess regression risks, and continuously improve testing strategies and quality standards.</li><li>Document defects clearly, communicate technical risks, and take ownership of quality throughout the development lifecycle.<br><br></li></ul><strong>Qualifications:<br><br></strong><ul><li>Bachelor's degree in Computer Science or a relevant field.</li><li>2–4 years of relevant software testing experience.</li><li>Experience with AI-assisted testing and development tools is highly desirable.<br><br></li></ul><strong>Job Specifications:<br><br></strong><ul><li>Strong analytical reasoning, critical thinking, risk-based testing, and boundary value analysis.</li><li>Hands-on familiarity with Postman, SQL, Jira, and browser developer tools.</li><li>Understanding of functional, exploratory, regression, integration, API, and end-to-end testing.</li><li>Knowledge of defect investigation, debugging, root-cause analysis, and test automation fundamentals.</li><li>Excellent written and verbal English, including requirement analysis and professional defect reporting.</li><li>Ability to identify assumptions, detect contradictions, evaluate competing explanations, and make evidence-based decisions.</li><li>Experience with ChatGPT, Microsoft Copilot, Claude, Gemini, Cursor, and GitHub Copilot is highly desirable.</li><li>Familiarity with Selenium, Python, JavaScript, PyCharm, Visual Studio, CI/CD pipelines, cloud environments, and distributed systems is preferred.</li><li>Knowledge of enterprise or SaaS application testing is an advantage.</li><li>Strong ownership, accountability, attention to detail, and independent problem-solving skills.<br><br></li></ul><strong>Perks &amp; Benefits:<br><br></strong><ul><li>Competitive salary package.</li><li>Provident Fund (PF).</li><li>Health and life insurance.</li><li>Paid leaves.</li><li>Professional development and career growth opportunities.</li><li>Supportive and collaborative work environment.</li><li>Paid certifications.<br><br></li></ul><strong>Location:</strong>Karachi, Sindh - Pakistan"
        }
      }
