      "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/paulcopplestone_today-supabase-is-announcing-150m-in-new-share-7511811435921072128-6ltf": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-27T18:55:57.495722+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "status": "active",
          "text": "Today, Supabase is announcing $150M in new funding, led by GIC, with CapitalG, IronArc Ventures, and Square Peg participating. We’re also welcoming Turso to Supabase.\n\nThe past year has been the fastest period of growth in Supabase’s history. We’re now adding more than 1M users and nearly 5M databases every month, and around 70% of new databases are being created by agents or AI-driven tools.\n\nAI is changing the economics of software creation. More people can build software, developers can build dramatically more of it, and agents are increasingly building alongside them.\n\nOur goal is to make Supabase the foundation for this agentic era. That means making it radically cheaper to start, while giving every application a clear path to scale.\nThat’s a big part of why we’re acquiring Turso.\n\nAs agents create more software, database demand will outpace the world’s current capacity. Turso has built an architecture that can handle vastly more small databases at a fraction of today’s cost. An agent can get an isolated database instantly, without requiring a dedicated machine for every workload.\n\nFor existing users, nothing changes. Supabase will continue building around Postgres, while Turso will continue its work on SQLite. Together, we’re creating something new that will bring the Supabase experience to every agent.\n\nThere’s a lot that brought our teams together: open source, developer experience, and a willingness to tackle hard infrastructure problems. We’re excited to welcome Glauber Costa , Pekka Enberg, and the entire Turso team to Supabase, with Glauber joining as Head of Agentic Services.\n\nThank you to GIC, CapitalG, IronArc, SquarePeg, and everyone who continues to support us. Most importantly, thank you to the Supabase community. You keep building faster than we expect, which means we have to keep doing the same.\n\nSri Muppidi has more on the news for the New York Times and we’ve shared more on the Supabase blog. Links in the comments.",
          "posted_at": "2026-10-02T15:36:49.683Z"
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/quratulain9274_were-hiring-associate-nodejs-developer-activity-7469663205590650881-SoEd": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-27T18:55:57.495722+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "status": "active",
          "text": "We're Hiring | Associate Node.js Developer\n\nExperience: Fresh Graduate – 1 Year\nLocation: DHA Phase 2 Extension, Karachi\n\nResponsibilities:\n• Develop and maintain backend applications using Node.js\n• Design, build, and integrate RESTful APIs\n• Troubleshoot, debug, and optimize application performance\n• Collaborate with cross-functional development teams\n• Work with databases and third-party service integrations\n\nRequirement:\n• Bachelor's degree in Computer Science or a related field\n• Strong understanding of JavaScript and Node.js fundamentals\n• Familiarity with Express.js and REST APIs\n• Basic knowledge of MongoDB and/or MySQL\n• Understanding of Git and version control systems is a plus\n• Strong analytical, problem-solving, and communication skills\n\nIf you're a fresh graduate looking to launch your career to grow, we'd love to hear from you!\n\nShare your resume at hr@resourcelinked.tech\nPlease mention \"Associate Node.js Developer\" in the subject line.",
          "posted_at": "2026-06-08T08:14:47.826Z"
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/alhazan-mubarak_fintech-nigeria-cloudcomputing-share-7516453508934422528-06Zm": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-27T18:54:13.063638+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "status": "active",
          "text": "I assumed AWS Local Zone in Lagos was the easy answer to the CBN localisation requirement. Then I sat down and read the documentation properly.\n\nIt isn't, at least not for the data layer.\n\nThere's no RDS in the Lagos Local Zone, so you'd be self-managing Postgres or MySQL on EC2. Also, Local Zones extend a parent Region (Lagos is linked to af-south-1), so EBS snapshots write to S3 in the parent Region by default. Local snapshots only work in Local Zones with S3 in-zone, and Lagos doesn't have that. So your backups end up in Cape Town.\n\nWhich leads to the bigger problem. There's no AWS Region in Nigeria. No Azure Region or Google Cloud Region either. If your payment database runs on a hyperscaler today, it's sitting in Ireland, Virginia or Cape Town — and so are your automated backups and your KMS keys.\n\nThe June circular requires payment transaction data generated in Nigeria to be stored and managed in Nigeria from 1 January 2027. That's under 90 days. For most teams, this isn't a settings change, because there's nowhere to point it at.\n\nThe harder question is what \"𝐬𝐭𝐨𝐫𝐞𝐝 𝐚𝐧𝐝 𝐦𝐚𝐧𝐚𝐠𝐞𝐝 𝐢𝐧 𝐍𝐢𝐠𝐞𝐫𝐢𝐚\" actually means in practice. Several law firms read it as covering the primary processing environment rather than just a copy held locally, which would mean backing up from a hyperscaler into Nigeria doesn't meet it. I put that question to Huawei Cloud directly and got the same answer, though they'd obviously have an interest in saying so.\n\nI've been working out how Nigerian startups can meet these requirements without needing a large infrastructure team or building everything from scratch.\n\nIf you're working through this at a Nigerian fintech or building infrastructure for one, I'd be glad to compare notes.\n\n#Fintech #Nigeria #CloudComputing #AWS",
          "posted_at": "2026-10-15T11:02:45.655Z"
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/betül-atiye-yalçın-56b2b4154_beytüşşebap-lokasyonumuzda-sorumluluk-almaya-share-7516098116530524160-C3k7": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-27T18:54:13.063638+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "status": "active",
          "text": "Beytüşşebap lokasyonumuzda sorumluluk almaya, sahada fark yaratmaya ve enerjisiyle değer katmaya hazır çalışma arkadaşlarımızı arıyoruz. ⚡",
